  "output_text": "{\"issues\":[],\"reason\":\"The construction is valid: the recurrence preserves positivity, odd parity, and the Pell-type identity; the resulting quadratic has discriminant t_k^2, so m_k is an integer root. The displayed equation then gives the required value 4, and strictly increasing n_k ensures infinitely many distinct pairs. The phrase “m_k optional +1” is an evident typographical artifact immediately corrected by the following explicit formula.\"}",
